      "content": "That's helpful, thanks. To make the debate really rigorous, my students need to see how these arguments were actually articulated to sound \"reasonable\" at the time. Regarding point 2, could you go deeper into the specific \"scientific\" claims they made about biological differences or intelligence? And for point 4, how did they specifically link racial preservation to the idea of social stability? If they can explain the supposed \"logic\" behind why they thought integration would lead to disorder, it'll help them understand the actual mindset of the 1920s. Just looking for the historical specifics of their reasoning.",
